use /lib
from /scope/open-projects import OpenProjectsScope
from /scope/prompt-mode/chat-input import ChatInputScope
from /scope/prompt-mode/modes import PromptModesScope

export shape MessageListScrollingShape:
    description:
        The latest task's table scrolls with its lock to the bottom off to
        start with, until switched on. Each open project keeps how far its
        latest task's table was scrolled and whether it was locked, and the
        rest of its message list as it was left, as the @{OpenProjectsScope}
        says, so switching back to it shows the list just as it was.

        However long the list of previous tasks grows, drawing it costs no more
        than drawing the tasks in view, so scrolling, animations, and new output
        stay smooth.

    scrollingPast:
        The previous tasks are not above the latest task in the message list
        but in the right sidebar's Tasks tab, so nothing lies past either end
        of the selected task's output: scrolling stops at its top and its
        bottom, with no stretch, glow, or crossing over. A task opened from
        the Tasks tab shows its output in the selected task's place, with a
        bar above it reading "Back to the latest task", which brings back the
        selected task's output scrolled just where it was left, its lock to
        the bottom as it was, as <Escape> in the message list does too.
